> gcd x^2-1, x^2+2x+1
gcd x^2 - 1, x^2 + 2x + 1
  = x + 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> gcd x^3-1, x^2-1
gcd x^3 - 1, x^2 - 1
  = x - 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> gcd 12, 18
gcd 12, 18
  = 6
> lcm x^2-1, x^2+2x+1
lcm x^2 - 1, x^2 + 2x + 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)^2
    = x^3 + x^2 - x - 1
  check: both divide it exactly
> lcm x^2-4, x^2-2x
lcm x^2 - 4, x^2 - 2x
  = x*(x - 2)*(x + 2)
    = x^3 - 4x
  check: both divide it exactly
> resultant x^2-2, x^2-3x+2
resultant x^2 - 2, x^2 - 3x + 2
  in x: -2
  nonzero: no common root
